### Job API Requests
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000/api/v1

#############################################
# Variables
#############################################

@job_id = <replace-with-actual-job-id>

#############################################
# Job Operations
#############################################

### Get a specific job by ID
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}

### Get audit logs for a job (structured, step-level milestones)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/audit

### Stream raw log lines for a job in real time (SSE)
### Use this while a job is `pending`/`processing` to tail progress in a UI;
### once a job reaches a terminal status, GET /audit is the right endpoint
### for structured metrics instead of re-reading the raw log.
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/logs
Accept: text/event-stream

#############################################
# Job Monitoring Examples
#############################################

### Monitor a specific job's progress
# 1. Get job details
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}

# 2. While pending/processing: stream live output
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/logs
Accept: text/event-stream

# 3. Once completed/failed: get audit logs for structured metrics
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/audit

# Expected job statuses: pending, processing, completed, failed

#############################################
# GET /jobs/:id/logs (SSE) — Frame Reference
#############################################

### Event frame format:
#   event: log
#   data: {"id","job_id","level":"info"|"warn"|"error","message","created_at"}
#
#   event: done
#   data: {"status": "completed" | "failed"}
#
# Behavior:
# - On connect, replays every JobLog row recorded so far as `event: log` frames.
# - If the job is already completed/failed, sends `event: done` and closes immediately.
# - Otherwise polls every `app.worker.logStreamPollIntervalMs` (default 1000ms)
#   for new lines and job-status changes, streaming new `event: log` frames,
#   until the job reaches a terminal state (`event: done`, connection closes)
#   or the client disconnects.
# - Backing store: the `JobLog` table, populated by the worker's
#   `withJobLogCapture` (src/helpers/job-log-capture.ts), which tees every
#   console.log/warn/error made while processing that job — including deep
#   inside IndexingService — without those modules needing DB access.

#############################################
# Common Audit Log Steps
#############################################

### Typical audit log steps for INDEX jobs:
# - JOB_CLAIM: Worker claimed the job
# - SCAN: File scanning completed
# - INITIALIZE_PROVIDERS: LLM and vector store initialization
# - PROCESS_FILES: File processing and chunking
# - BUILD_GRAPH: Dependency graph construction
# - INDEXING: Overall indexing process
# - JOB_COMPLETE: Job finished successfully
# - JOB_FAILED: Job failed (if error occurred)

### Typical audit log steps for REFRESH jobs (current, full-scan):
# - JOB_CLAIM: Worker claimed the job
# - COLLECTION_RESET: Qdrant collection dropped before the full re-scan
#   (src/helpers/collection-reset.ts), so stale chunks from files removed
#   or renamed on disk since the last run cannot linger.
# - REFRESH: Refresh process (full-scan today for every source type)
# - JOB_COMPLETE: Job finished successfully
# - JOB_FAILED: Job failed (if error occurred)

### Typical audit log steps for REFRESH jobs (once Git Integration + Delta-Aware
### Refresh phases land — GIT-sourced repositories only; LOCAL repositories
### keep doing the full-scan + COLLECTION_RESET behavior above indefinitely):
# - JOB_CLAIM: Worker claimed the job
# - DELTA_DETECTION: Git diff and change analysis
# - SCAN: Delta file scanning
# - INITIALIZE_PROVIDERS: LLM and vector store initialization
# - PROCESS_FILES: Changed file processing
# - BUILD_GRAPH: Dependency graph construction
# - INDEXING: Overall indexing process
# - JOB_COMPLETE: Job finished successfully
# - JOB_FAILED: Job failed (if error occurred)

#############################################
# Job Status Examples
#############################################

### Example: Check if a job completed successfully
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}

# Look for:
# - status: "completed" (success) or "failed" (error)
# - completed_at: timestamp when job finished
# - error_message: null (success) or error text (failure)
# - retry_count: number of retry attempts

### Example: Get detailed metrics from audit logs
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/jobs/{{job_id}}/audit

# Look for metrics in completed audit log entries:
# - SCAN: { fileCount, durationMs }
# - INITIALIZE_PROVIDERS: { embeddingModel, enrichmentModel, existingPoints }
# - PROCESS_FILES: { successfulFiles, failedFiles, totalFiles, durationMs, totalChunks, enrichedChunks }
# - BUILD_GRAPH: { graphNodeCount, graphEdgeCount }
# - COLLECTION_RESET: { collectionName }
# - INDEXING: { chunkCount, fileCount, durationMs, graphNodeCount, graphEdgeCount }
# - REFRESH: { chunkCount, fileCount, durationMs, graphNodeCount, graphEdgeCount }
# - DELTA_DETECTION: { changedFiles, chunksToCreate, chunksToDelete, chunksToReindex, deltaDetectionTimeMs }
